    feat(sprint-11): US-11.3 chosen_r early-stop log-parsing wrapper
    
    Ships the Rule A plateau-break detector from Sprint 8 insights-addressed.md
    as a subprocess.Popen log-parsing wrapper around mlx_lm_lora training.
    Halts DPO when train_chosen_r drops below 50% of its trailing-5-window mean
    for 2 consecutive eval steps — the production-cheap proxy for the Anthropic
    2507.21509 persona-vector projection signal (full activation projection
    deferred to Sprint 12).
    
    - scripts/dpo_early_stop.py: ChosenRPlateauDetector + parse_iter_line +
      run_with_early_stop subprocess wrapper. Emits structured JSON event
      with {first_breach_iter, stopped_iter, promoted_iter, trailing_mean,
      threshold}; writes .early_stop sentinel + event log on fire.
    - scripts/finetune-gemma.py: --early-stopping-signal {chosen_r,none}
      CLI flag (default chosen_r); routes run_dpo() subprocess through the
      wrapper when enabled; defaults to 'none' on synthesized Namespaces to
      preserve back-compat with Sprint 7/8 tests.
    - tests/fixtures/sprint8_dpo80_log.jsonl: distilled 16-record JSONL
      from /tmp/dpo80.log (Sprint 8 Smoke #3).
    - tests/test_dpo_early_stop.py: 13 deterministic offline tests covering
      AC-11.3.1..5 — fixture replay asserts first_breach_iter=65,
      stopped_iter=70, promoted_iter=60.

